{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AHsgLcTCKVmGNPcGaMU6Ja","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Runbook — what to run, in what order\n2\t\n3\tEverything in this repo is built and tested offline against contract **v0.3.0**.\n4\tWhat remains is running it against a real model, which has still never happened.\n5\t\n6\tRun from the repo root. Every command uses the venv by absolute path.\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## 0. Baseline (30 seconds, no credential)\n11\t\n12\t```bash\n13\tbash setup.sh\n14\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n15\t.venv/bin/python demo.py --replay\n16\t```\n17\t\n18\tExpected: the suite green, and the demo walking eight steps ending\n19\t`8 steps · 8 as scripted · no spend recorded`. If either fails, stop — nothing\n20\tbelow is meaningful on a broken baseline.\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## 1. The Claude subscription account\n25\t\n26\tThe local POC defaults to Claude Code using `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. Keep that\n27\ttoken in the machine-level secrets file, not this project's `.env`, and source\n28\tthe machine-level file before running the commands below.\n29\t\n30\tCheck what is actually in play:\n31\t\n32\t```bash\n33\t.venv/bin/python authcheck.py\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\tExpected: `Provider: Claude Code subscription account`, the token marked set,\n37\tand Claude reporting logged in. The diagnostic never prints the token.\n38\t\n39\t`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` remains an opt-in compatibility path for\n40\tAPI deployments, but it is not the local POC path.\n41\t\n42\tThe subscription route is pinned to `claude-sonnet-4-6`; the harness passes\n43\tthat concrete model to `claude --model` and records it in reports.\n44\t`CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL` is an explicit experimental override. Changing it starts\n45\ta different evaluation and cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another\n46\tmodel.\n47\t\n48\tThen, in order — each step is cheap and each one gates the next:\n49\t\n50\t```bash\n51\t.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live -m live -q\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tThree cases and a control-envelope check using account-plan quota. The Anthropic\n55\tSDK-only cache-counter test is skipped because Claude CLI does not expose those\n56\tcounters. A pass here is the first evidence that the local account path works\n57\tend to end.\n58\t\n59\tStart with the cases that exposed request and routing instability:\n60\t\n61\t```bash\n62\t.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 \\\n63\t  --case answer/VC-POC-01 \\\n64\t  --case answer/VC-POC-03 \\\n65\t  --case answer/VC-POC-04 \\\n66\t  --max-trials 3\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\tContinue the same checkpoint in a later account window using the path printed\n70\tby the runner:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a975106-0ac1-4d93-9678-77f65344e100","uuid":"4bc4fc14-fb12-41ae-a2cc-6b86ecdc4d81","timestamp":"2026-09-27T13:14:53.397Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/RUNBOOK.md","content":"# Runbook — what to run, in what order\n\nEverything in this repo is built and tested offline against contract **v0.3.0**.\nWhat remains is running it against a real model, which has still never happened.\n\nRun from the repo root. Every command uses the venv by absolute path.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Baseline (30 seconds, no credential)\n\n```bash\nbash setup.sh\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n.venv/bin/python demo.py --replay\n```\n\nExpected: the suite green, and the demo walking eight steps ending\n`8 steps · 8 as scripted · no spend recorded`. If either fails, stop — nothing\nbelow is meaningful on a broken baseline.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Claude subscription account\n\nThe local POC defaults to Claude Code using `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. Keep that\ntoken in the machine-level secrets file, not this project's `.env`, and source\nthe machine-level file before running the commands below.\n\nCheck what is actually in play:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python authcheck.py\n```\n\nExpected: `Provider: Claude Code subscription account`, the token marked set,\nand Claude reporting logged in. The diagnostic never prints the token.\n\n`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` remains an opt-in compatibility path for\nAPI deployments, but it is not the local POC path.\n\nThe subscription route is pinned to `claude-sonnet-4-6`; the harness passes\nthat concrete model to `claude --model` and records it in reports.\n`CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL` is an explicit experimental override. Changing it starts\na different evaluation and cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another\nmodel.\n\nThen, in order — each step is cheap and each one gates the next:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live -m live -q\n```\n\nThree cases and a control-envelope check using account-plan quota. The Anthropic\nSDK-only cache-counter test is skipped because Claude CLI does not expose those\ncounters. A pass here is the first evidence that the local account path works\nend to end.\n\nStart with the cases that exposed request and routing instability:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m evals.live --k 3 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-01 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-03 \\\n  --case answer/VC-POC-04 \\\n  --max-trials 3\n```\n\nContinue the same checkpoint in a later account window using the path printed\nby the runner:","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":213}}}
