{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CcnKq7antXP5zoSJorn5of","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# PreToolUse hook for mcp__github__create_pull_request.\n#\n# Blocks PR creation unless the branch satisfies the repo's release-notes CI gate\n# (.github workflow \"release-notes\"). Mirrors that gate locally so a PR fails HERE,\n# before it is opened, instead of after a red CI run. Emits a PreToolUse deny\n# decision (permissionDecision: deny) with an actionable reason.\n#\n# Base ref override (for testing): RELEASE_NOTES_BASE=<ref>.\n#\n# Otherwise the base is read from the PR being created, matching what CI does\n# (pr-checks.yml uses BASE=\"origin/${{ github.base_ref }}\"). Hardcoding origin/main\n# here made the hook disagree with the gate it mirrors on any stacked PR — a branch\n# based on another open branch was denied for every release note in the stack below\n# it, notes CI would never have counted. origin/main remains the fallback when the\n# tool input carries no base.\nset -uo pipefail\n\ndeny() {\n    # $1 must contain no double quotes (kept literal in the JSON below).\n    printf '{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecision\":\"deny\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"%s\"}}\\n' \"$1\"\n    exit 0\n}\n\n# PreToolUse hooks receive the tool call as JSON on stdin. Read the PR's base\n# branch from it; python3 over a regex because the field is a JSON string and the\n# body around it is arbitrary prose.\nPR_BASE=\"\"\nif [ ! -t 0 ]; then\n    PR_BASE=\"$(python3 -c 'import json,sys\ntry:\n    d = json.load(sys.stdin)\nexcept Exception:\n    sys.exit(0)\ni = d.get(\"tool_input\") or {}\nb = i.get(\"base\")\nprint(b if isinstance(b, str) else \"\")' 2>/dev/null || true)\"\nfi\n\nif [ -n \"${RELEASE_NOTES_BASE:-}\" ]; then\n    BASE=\"$RELEASE_NOTES_BASE\"\nelif [ -n \"$PR_BASE\" ]; then\n    BASE=\"origin/$PR_BASE\"\n    git fetch origin \"$PR_BASE\" --depth=1 -q 2>/dev/null || true\nelse\n    BASE=\"origin/main\"\nfi\n\ngit fetch origin main --depth=1 -q 2>/dev/null || true\ngit rev-parse --verify -q \"$BASE\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || BASE=\"$(git merge-base HEAD origin/main 2>/dev/null || echo HEAD)\"\n\n# 1. Never bump VERSION in a PR — release.yml assigns it at merge. Compare\n# against the MERGE-BASE, not the main tip: release.yml bumps VERSION on every\n# merge, so a branch cut before the latest release would otherwise be denied\n# for a bump it never made.\nMB=\"$(git merge-base HEAD \"$BASE\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"$BASE\")\"\nBASE_V=\"$(git show \"$MB:VERSION\" 2>/dev/null | tr -d '[:space:]' || true)\"\nHEAD_V=\"$(tr -d '[:space:]' < VERSION 2>/dev/null || true)\"\nif [ -n \"$BASE_V\" ] && [ \"$BASE_V\" != \"$HEAD_V\" ]; then\n    deny \"Blocked: PR modifies VERSION ($BASE_V -> $HEAD_V). Versions are assigned at merge by release.yml — revert the bump and add releases/_next/<slug>.md instead.\"\nfi\n\n# 2. Never add versioned notes — those are generated at merge.\nADDED_FINAL=\"$(git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A \"$BASE\"...HEAD -- 'releases/v*.md' 2>/dev/null)\"\nif [ -n \"$ADDED_FINAL\" ]; then\n    deny \"Blocked: PR adds versioned notes ($ADDED_FINAL). Those are generated at merge — put the notes in releases/_next/<slug>.md instead.\"\nfi\n\n# 3. Exactly one releases/_next/*.md must be added.\nADDED=\"$(git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A \"$BASE\"...HEAD -- 'releases/_next/*.md' 2>/dev/null)\"\nCOUNT=\"$(printf '%s' \"$ADDED\" | grep -c . || true)\"\nif [ \"$COUNT\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    deny \"Blocked: no releases/_next/*.md added. Every PR is a release — copy releases/_template.md to releases/_next/<slug>.md (keep the vNEXT heading, do NOT touch VERSION), add a Type line and a Local deployment section, commit it, then retry.\"\nfi\nif [ \"$COUNT\" -gt 1 ]; then\n    deny \"Blocked: PR adds $COUNT files under releases/_next/ — one PR, one release, one notes file.\"\nfi\n\n# 4. That file needs a Type line and the mandatory sections (CI-enforced).\nif ! grep -Eiq '^\\*\\*Type:\\*\\* *(patch|minor|major) *$' \"$ADDED\"; then\n    deny \"Blocked: $ADDED needs a Type line: '**Type:** patch|minor|major' (pick exactly one) — it drives the version bump at merge.\"\nfi\nif ! grep -q '^## Local deployment' \"$ADDED\"; then\n    deny \"Blocked: $ADDED has no '## Local deployment' section (write 'Nothing to do.' if true).\"\nfi\nif ! grep -q '^## Manual steps' \"$ADDED\"; then\n    deny \"Blocked: $ADDED has no '## Manual steps' section (write 'Nothing to do.' if none).\"\nfi\nif ! grep -q '^## Verification' \"$ADDED\"; then\n    deny \"Blocked: $ADDED has no '## Verification' section — post-merge checks as copy-pasteable commands.\"\nfi\n# Prose-only checks are rejected: Verification needs a fenced bash block.\nif ! awk '/^## Verification/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f' \"$ADDED\" | grep -q '^```bash'; then\n    deny \"Blocked: $ADDED '## Verification' needs at least one fenced bash code block of commands run against main after merge.\"\nfi\n\nexit 0","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a975106-0ac1-4d93-9678-77f65344e100","uuid":"14a45d1c-4a3d-436d-85bb-10e4cdebe070","timestamp":"2026-09-27T13:15:01.984Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# PreToolUse hook for mcp__github__create_pull_request.\n#\n# Blocks PR creation unless the branch satisfies the repo's release-notes CI gate\n# (.github workflow \"release-notes\"). Mirrors that gate locally so a PR fails HERE,\n# before it is opened, instead of after a red CI run. Emits a PreToolUse deny\n# decision (permissionDecision: deny) with an actionable reason.\n#\n# Base ref override (for testing): RELEASE_NOTES_BASE=<ref>.\n#\n# Otherwise the base is read from the PR being created, matching what CI does\n# (pr-checks.yml uses BASE=\"origin/${{ github.base_ref }}\"). Hardcoding origin/main\n# here made the hook disagree with the gate it mirrors on any stacked PR — a branch\n# based on another open branch was denied for e