{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NYoQpr4kXGPEyVYD5wYztR","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/releases/_next/claude-account-usage.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a975106-0ac1-4d93-9678-77f65344e100","uuid":"9d192259-cb8d-4277-80cd-88b395dfc286","timestamp":"2026-09-27T13:15:14.289Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/releases/_next/claude-account-usage.md","content":"# vNEXT — Record real Claude account token usage, including cache and helper models\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-27\n**PR:** #N\n**Type:** patch\n\n## Summary\n\nThe Claude subscription-account transport (`harness/claude_account_cli.py`)\npreviously returned every `ModelResponse` with no `usage`, so account-mode\nrequests were recorded as all-zero tokens and the ADR-006 cache-hit\nregression view could never fire on the local POC path. It now maps the CLI\nsuccess envelope's `usage`/`modelUsage` into a populated `RequestUsage`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `harness/claude_account_cli.py::_request_usage`, a pure helper that\n  maps the CLI's `usage` block (`input_tokens`, `output_tokens`,\n  `cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`) into a\n  `RequestUsage` with `input_tokens` set to base input plus cache read/write,\n  per the genai-prices convention `harness/usage.py` already assumes.\n- When the envelope's `modelUsage` map names a main model and any helper\n  model, their counts are summed into the returned aggregate, and a\n  per-model, integer-only, model-name-keyed breakdown is recorded in\n  `RequestUsage.details` (no `LlmRequestRecord` schema change).\n- A missing or partial `usage` block yields zeroed usage instead of raising\n  (ADR-005 telemetry-never-fails).\n- Neither the returned usage nor its `details` ever contains the CLI\n  `result` text or any token/credential — only numeric counts and model\n  names.\n- Corrected `RUNBOOK.md` §1, which claimed the Claude CLI does not expose\n  cache counters; it now reflects that the CLI returns\n  `cache_read_input_tokens`/`cache_creation_input_tokens` and per-model\n  `modelUsage`, which the harness records.\n\n## Local deployment\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Manual steps\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py -q\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage.py -q\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n```\n\nExpected: all three commands exit zero with no failures or errors; the new\n`_request_usage` tests (usage mapping, helper-model aggregation, no-raw/no-secret,\nmissing-usage tolerance, end-to-end populated usage) pass alongside the\nexisting suite.\n\n## Rollback\n\n`git revert` this commit; no data migration or schema change is involved.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
